:"What is the trace of $\\operatorname{diag}(3,0,-2)$?","options":["$-6$","$1$","$5$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d5125a36e99e8d4efbf9c128"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,5)$, what is $D\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}x+2\\\\y+5\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}5x\\\\2y\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2x+5y\\\\2x+5y\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2x\\\\5y\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"353481a3cc712d2dd6d3a0fc"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,3)$ and $E=\\operatorname{diag}(4,-1)$, what is $D+E$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}6&1\\\\1&2\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\operatorname{diag}(8,-3)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(6,2)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(2,3,4,-1)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3068cd1fd9e2f2cb0bbe56af"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The eigenvalues of a diagonal matrix are:","options":["always all equal to $1$","the sum of its entries","exactly its diagonal entries","its off-diagonal entries"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cac9c6d387c1efbe6b08aacf"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What stays diagonal when two diagonal matrices of the same size are added?","options":["The sum, because off-diagonal zeros remain zero.","Only the determinant, not the matrix.","The inverse of every diagonal matrix.","Nothing unless the diagonal entries are all distinct."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5856b9a858aec70468de5d7d"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What condition makes a diagonal matrix invertible?","options":["The trace is positive.","All off-diagonal entries are one.","At least one diagonal entry is zero.","Every diagonal entry is nonzero."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4567c5419d10518355a2fbca"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,-3,4)$ and $E=\\operatorname{diag}(5,1,0)$, what is the diagonal of $DE$?","options":["$7,-2,4$","$10,-3,0$","$5,-3,0$","$10,3,4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fafd7f790ddae98dc75d31c0"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,-1,5)$, which vector is $D(1,2,3)^T$?","options":["$(2,-1,5)^T$","$(2,1,8)^T$","$(1,-2,15)^T$","$(2,-2,15)^T$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2ecc003f7ada528dfee29ead"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which diagonal matrix is singular?","options":["$\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,3)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(-2,7,8)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(4,2,1)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(2,0,5)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"46c4a7d8104852d71c0d3e8f"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $D=\\operatorname{diag}(d_1,\\dots,d_n)$, the power $D^{k}$ equals:","options":["$\\operatorname{diag}(kd_1,\\dots,kd_n)$","$kD$","$\\operatorname{diag}(d_1,\\dots,d_n)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(d_1^{k},\\dots,d_n^{k})$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"313bc16461f747df6d561640"},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What can go wrong if one diagonal entry is zero?","options":["The trace is undefined.","The matrix stops being square.","All other diagonal entries become zero, in all instances without exception.","One coordinate direction is collapsed, so the matrix is not invertible."],"answer_mode":"server","f